title: Saved by Grace Through Faith – The Doctrine of Salvation
description: Saved by grace through faith in Christ, without works: an overview of the teaching on salvation in the King James Bible, from sin and the gospel to the blood, imputed righteousness, repentance, James 2 and adoption.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-salvation.html

# An overview of the whole topic, built from the author's teachings in studies/data/topics/salvation.json,
# one or two slides for each theme. Every paragraph is the author's own wording, trimmed.

=== Introduction
# from the topic summary in salvation.json
--- Saved by Grace Through Faith [title]
overline: Doctrine · Salvation
heading: Saved by Grace Through Faith
sub: Saved by grace through faith in Christ, without works.
refs: Ephesians 2:8-9; John 3:16; Romans 10:13
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 6040, 12272
--- The doctrine
big: Ephesians 2:8-9 | mark: For by grace are ye saved through faith
lead: There is no doubt we are saved from our sins and Hell by faith alone, by grace alone, in Christ alone. That God’s grace extends to all men.
p: This is the Gospel. There is nothing more to it. There can be nothing less.

=== All have sinned
# from 17714, 10750
--- None righteous, no, not one
scripture: Romans 3:10-12
p: It serves as a universal appeal to the need for the gospel, and the reconciliation of fallen men with a holy God. There is none good but God. All have gone astray.
tile: 1 | All have sinned.
tile: 2 | All deserve death.
tile: 3 | Jews under the law.
tile: 4 | Gentiles without the law.
refs: Romans 3:23; Romans 6:23

=== The gospel that must be believed
# from 11404, 5309
--- What one must understand to be saved
- If you don’t believe you are a sinner, or that as a sinner you deserve Hell and death, you won’t accept the Gospel.
- If you don’t believe that salvation from the wages of your sin, Hell and death, is a free gift, given by God’s grace and not of yourself, you cannot turn to believe the Gospel.
- If you don’t believe that Jesus is the Son of God, Who was made flesh, lived a sinless life, was crucified, buried and risen again, that we may have remission of sin and eternal life, you can’t believe and be saved.
- If you don’t accept the gift from God in Jesus name, calling upon the name of the Lord to forgive you, a sinner, you cannot be saved.
callout: The gospel of grace and reconciliation by which we believe and are saved, is a concrete understandable and specific thing, spelled out by God hundreds of different ways throughout the Bible. [[1 Corinthians 15:3-4]]

# from 3071
--- What must I do to be saved?
scripture: Acts 16:30-31 | mark: Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be saved
p: This is the fundamental question. This is the doctrine of the Gospel being asked for, and Paul answers, not with long-winded theological points or esoteric hints at salvation being some sort of Gnostic journey.
p: We are saved by faith alone, plus nothing minus nothing.

=== Grace, not works
# from 10780, 10778, 8964
--- To him that worketh not
big: Romans 4:5
p: Works has nothing to do with salvation. God doesn’t owe us salvation. Our works, no matter how good we think they are, can never offset our sin, and the wages thereof.
p: Grace is the unearned, unmerited, undeserved gift given by God from His mercy and love. **Debt is deserved. Grace is undeserved.**

# from 12272, 4511
--- Trusting anything but Christ
panel-warn: Anything else | If you are trusting in traditions, rites, your sacrifices, prayers to saints, carnal ordinances and sacraments, doing good works or turning from your sins to save you, you are assuredly perishing.
panel-warn: Even partially | If they trust in their circumcision to justify them, even partially, then Christ will profit them nothing. [[Galatians 5:2-4]]
panel: The finished work of Christ | The only salvation is by grace of God, the unmerited favor He extends to all, that whosoever believes on His Son… Period. Plus nothing. Minus nothing.

=== The blood atonement
# from 16360
--- Only the blood atones
panel-warn: None of these | Turning your life around, repenting of sin, joining a church, getting water baptized, making Jesus the Lord of your life, seeing real change, sacraments and good deeds... None of these things satisfy the price of sin.
big: Romans 3:25 | mark: propitiation through faith in his blood
p: Only the blood of a holy God offered in our place and sprinkled on the mercy seat can atone for our sin and justify us before God. That is the only propitiation. [[Hebrews 9:12]] [[Hebrews 9:22]]

# from 10791
--- While we were yet sinners
big: Romans 5:8
p: That when we were still enemies, working iniquities, dead in sin, God reconciled us through the death of His Son. God loved His enemies, and offered the free gift of salvation by the shedding of blood of His only begotten Son.
p: Think about this, for in it is the righteousness of God. [[Romans 5:9-10]]

=== Imputed righteousness
# from 1714
--- An exchange
big: 2 Corinthians 5:21
p: Jesus took on our sin and paid the price for all of it. He was the propitiation. The ransom. The sacrifice.
p: By believing this, we take on His righteousness. His blood washes us clean. We are clothed in white of his perfection, our sins forgotten.
take: It is an exchange. That is the testament.

# from 10778, 10782
--- Abraham believed God
fig: Counted unto him for righteousness | Genesis 15:6; Romans 4:3
p: If it were of works, that means God would be indebted to us. To pay us for our works. That we were owed.
p: Abraham did not receive the ordinance of circumcision until decades after his believing God’s promise, and being saved by that faith. [[Romans 4:10-11]]

=== Repentance is a change of mind
# from 2015, 805, 5309, 2839
--- What the Bible means by repent
lit: “Repent of your sins” | Jonah 3:10 | Here we get the biblical definition of repent, God changing His mind, AND the acknowledgement that “turning from their evil ways” ie “Repenting of sin” = works.
rev: Turning to the Lord | Acts 11:18; Acts 11:21 | They have identical meaning. There is no implied “...from sin.” It is Biblical repentance, *turning to the Lord.*
p: There is no clear verse that spells out a Doctrine that says that we must give up sin or be willing to give up sin in order to believe and be saved. Repentance is a changing of mind or turning from one thing to another.
callout: Biblical repentance in relation to salvation is always this; turning from whatever else you are relying on, or whatever delusion that you hold that conflicts with the good news of Jesus Christ, and turning towards God and acceptance of this truth.

# from 11437, 806
--- Saved, though still sinners
p: Saying “real repentance WILL mean you turn from sin, and WILL walk in the Spirit,” is false. We must pick up our cross daily. It is a choice to engage in sanctification. But salvation is of Christ, not ourselves.
p: The spirit does work in us the more we grow closer to God, to help remove the thorns in our hearts as we become more sanctified, praise God! But we are saved just as we are, though we still are sinners.
callout-honest: Don’t let the misunderstanding about repentance be the stumbling block that keeps you from His grace.

=== Justified before men
# from 10779, 6040
--- James 2 and Romans 4
lit: Justified by works? | James 2:21 | The misuse of James 2 to teach a false gospel of works is one of the great stumbling blocks to salvation and faith.
rev: Not before God | Romans 4:2-3 | Scripture says it was faith that justified Abraham to God.
p: By comparing scripture with scripture we see that there is no contradiction, only context. That Paul is writing of justification before God in grace, while James is writing of justification before man, by doing good works in faith.
p: This is the Biblical Doctrine of good works. That they which *have believed*, past tense, might do them and be profitable to others. [[Titus 3:8]]

=== Adopted sons and heirs
# from 6578, 5281
--- The sons of God
big: John 1:12
p: We who are saved by grace through faith are adopted as sons of God, heirs to His promise and the Kingdom of Heaven.
p: Our entrance to the kingdom is free, for we are at Liberty in Christ. We pay nothing, not our works or labors or deeds. It is a gift of God given to all who believe. [[Matthew 17:25-26]] [[Romans 8:16-17]]

# from 13524, 11140, 11404
--- Passed from death unto life
big: John 5:24
p: This is why we who believe on Him that is faithful and true may know we have eternal life. That we are sealed unto redemption by His Spirit. That He testifies within us. That we may have that blessed assurance. Eternally adopted sons and daughters of God.
panel-warn: Lose the gift? | If you think that anything you do can justify you, or to lose that free gift, given by God by grace through faith in Christ, you aren’t saved.

=== Closing
# from 215
--- Confess and believe
scripture: Romans 10:9-10
p: If you believe in your heart that God loved you so much, He sent His only begotten son to die for your sin and be raised again, then confess this with your mouth in prayer, calling upon Jesus’ name, and be saved. Knowing that blessed assurance of eternal security, never to be lost or taken away.

# from 17714, 11404, 6040, 16360, 1714, 805, 10779, 6578
--- Saved by grace through faith
point: All have sinned | There is none good but God. All have gone astray.
point: The gospel | Christ made flesh, sinless, crucified, buried and risen again, that we may have remission of sin and eternal life.
point: Grace, not works | Works has nothing to do with salvation. God doesn’t owe us salvation.
point: The blood | Only the blood of a holy God offered in our place can atone for our sin.
point: Imputed righteousness | It is an exchange. That is the testament.
point: Repentance | A changing of mind, turning towards God.
point: James 2 | Justified before God by faith, before men by works.
point: Adopted sons | A gift of God given to all who believe, never to be lost or taken away.

